<h2>06 · Retained failures and remaining work</h2>
<ul>{report.openReleaseGates?.map(x=><li>{x}</li>)}</ul>
<p>The original component report retains its rejected wire placement and unresolved rare-event comparisons. Later passing surface checks do not relabel those failures. The first finer induction mesh failed the 10⁻¹⁰ true-residual gate at 1.3595969434732396 × 10⁻⁵ after 16,000 iterations. RCM reordering also failed. The original vertex-load implementation passed the algebraic gate but produced per-cell field-transfer differences of 14.0–39.7%, above the unchanged 5% mesh criterion. Four-point volume quadrature reduces these differences to 0.6–10.6%; two cells still fail. The eleven-point degree-four rule gives 0.55%, 5.28%, 10.10% and 6.12%, with three failures. Those coarse meshes remain rejected. Conservative factor 2 versus 4 then gave a 5.3361% difference for one cell and remains rejected. Factor 3 still failed at 5.52%; separating directions found axial errors below 0.9% but one radial error of 5.59%. The subsequent radial-4 to radial-5 comparison still failed two cells at 6.7270% and 6.1171%. An unpublished fixed-parent subdivision attempt failed an axial comparison at 5.7252%; its temporary raw artifacts were lost when the execution workspace disappeared. Those observed values remain explicitly separated from recovered raw evidence. Current qualification uses the reconstructed subdivision method and both seed cohorts described above. Only newly executed studies can qualify it.</p>
<pre>{JSON.stringify(report.retainedFailures,null,2)}</pre>
<details><summary>Supplemental source-integration diagnostics</summary><pre>{JSON.stringify({fourPoint:report.inductionQuadrature?.rows,elevenPoint:report.inductionQuadrature11?.rows,fineDirect:report.inductionDirect},null,2)}</pre></details>
<p>The 12 magnetic membrane checks compare native NEURON and two time-step halvings at 0, 10 and 100 A, including a whole-cell block. These fixtures do not fire. The earlier predeclared positive stress grid reached propagation only at 100 million A in the weak axial-coil fixture. The current report below must repeat that stress qualification with the selected production field. Its native/time-step and spatial conduction/recording tests check implementation at the same absolute drive. That artificial current is outside the 0–100 A interface and supplies no feasibility or operating threshold claim.</p>
